# Copy to tests/catalyst-center/.env (gitignored) and chmod 600 it, to run
# the live Catalyst Center end-to-end tests (tests/e2e/catalyst_test.go): the
# catalyst_center sync plugin against a real Cisco Catalyst Center. They sign
# in, page the device inventory, classify each device, check the controller
# itself lands in inventory as a device, check a second sync changes nothing,
# and check a wrong password is refused. They only read the controller.
#
# With only PLEIADES_E2E_DNAC set, they use Cisco's always-on DevNet Catalyst
# Center sandbox and the read-only account DevNet publishes for it; the three
# settings below point them at another controller (a reserved sandbox, or
# your own). One test signs in with a wrong password on purpose, which a
# controller that locks accounts after failed logins counts.
#
# The tests are behind the integration build tag and this opt-in, so CI never
# depends on a third-party sandbox. Run them with the variables exported, from
# the module root:
#
#   go test -tags integration -race ./tests/e2e/ -run Catalyst -count=1 -v
#
# The opt-in: any value runs the tests.
PLEIADES_E2E_DNAC=1
# The controller's base URL; leave empty for the always-on sandbox.
PLEIADES_E2E_DNAC_ENDPOINT=
# Its login; leave both empty for the sandbox's published read-only account.
PLEIADES_E2E_DNAC_USER=
PLEIADES_E2E_DNAC_PASS=
